  "question": {
    "text": "In the extraction of copper, its sulphide ore is heated in a reverberatory furnace after mixing with silica to:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "separate <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>CuO</mi></math>&nbsp;as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CuSiO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "remove calcium as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CaSiO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "decrease the temperature needed for roasting of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Cu</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "remove <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>FeO</mi></math>&nbsp;as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>FeSiO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>In actual practice, the ore is heated in reverberatory furnace after mixing with silica. In the furnace, iron oxide &#39;slags off&#39; as iron silicate and copper is produced in the form copper matte. This contains&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Cu</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>FeS</mi></math>.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>FeO</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>SiO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#10230;</mo><msub><mi>FeSiO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math></p>"
  }
}